ToplevelActivity: deliver intents arriving at a running activity

An activity only receives its launch intent in onCreate. When a VIEW
intent resolves to an already-running task (the standard case for custom
URI schemes: browsers add FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK, so an OAuth/OIDC
redirect bounced back from a browser fronts the existing task), Android
delivers it through onNewIntent — which ToplevelActivity did not
implement, so the URI was silently dropped. Forward it to
GdkContext.open like onCreate does. Only effective together with a
non-"standard" launchMode (e.g. singleTask): with "standard", the
task-to-front path delivers no intent at all.

diff --git a/gdk/android/glue/java/org/gtk/android/ToplevelActivity.java b/gdk/android/glue/java/org/gtk/android/ToplevelActivity.java
--- a/gdk/android/glue/java/org/gtk/android/ToplevelActivity.java
+++ b/gdk/android/glue/java/org/gtk/android/ToplevelActivity.java
@@ -489,6 +489,23 @@
 		});
 	}

+	@Override
+	protected void onNewIntent(Intent intent) {
+		super.onNewIntent(intent);
+		setIntent(intent);
+
+		if (intent.getData() == null)
+			return;
+
+		String hint = "";
+		if (intent.getAction() != null) {
+			String[] action = intent.getAction().split("\\.");
+			hint = action[action.length - 1].toLowerCase();
+		}
+		final String fhint = hint;
+		GlibContext.runOnMain(() -> GdkContext.open(intent.getData(), fhint));
+	}
+
